["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>A covey thinks as a group: watch, call, run, burst, scatter, regroup. Learn the script and you know their next move before they make it.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Table of California quail calls. Assembly call, chi CA go or cu CA cow, loudest on the middle note: given by a bird separated from the covey or as the covey moves. Contact calls, soft clucks and pips, while feeding. Alarm, sharp pit pit, when danger is close. Advertising call, one loud cow, by unpaired males in spring. Fighting call, squill, by males sorting rank in spring. 70 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Quail calls and what they mean</text>\n<text x=\"70\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Call</text>\n<text x=\"185\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sounds like</text>\n<text x=\"320\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">When</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"60\" width=\"120\" height=\"38\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"70\" y=\"85\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Assembly</text>\n<rect x=\"134\" y=\"60\" width=\"256\" height=\"38\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"190\" y=\"85\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">&quot;chi CA go&quot;</text>\n<text x=\"322\" y=\"85\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Lost, or covey moving</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"104\" width=\"120\" height=\"38\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"70\" y=\"129\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Contact</text>\n<rect x=\"134\" y=\"104\" width=\"256\" height=\"38\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"190\" y=\"129\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">soft clucks, pips</text>\n<text x=\"322\" y=\"129\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Feeding together</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"148\" width=\"120\" height=\"38\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#a33b2a\"/>\n<text x=\"70\" y=\"173\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Alarm</text>\n<rect x=\"134\" y=\"148\" width=\"256\" height=\"38\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"190\" y=\"173\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">sharp &quot;pit pit&quot;</text>\n<text x=\"322\" y=\"173\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Danger close</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"192\" width=\"120\" height=\"38\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n<text x=\"70\" y=\"217\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Advertising</text>\n<rect x=\"134\" y=\"192\" width=\"256\" height=\"38\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"190\" y=\"217\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">one loud &quot;cow&quot;</text>\n<text x=\"322\" y=\"217\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Spring, unpaired male</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"236\" width=\"120\" height=\"38\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"70\" y=\"261\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Fighting</text>\n<rect x=\"134\" y=\"236\" width=\"256\" height=\"38\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"190\" y=\"261\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">&quot;squill&quot;</text>\n<text x=\"322\" y=\"261\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Spring, males sort rank</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">From bird guides (70%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Quail talk all day: assembly, contact, alarm, advertising and fighting calls <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>The assembly call, \"chi CA go\", is the one to learn first <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the calls in full</summary><ul><li>Assembly call: three syllables, loudest on the middle one (\"cu CA cow\" or \"chi CA go\"). Given when a bird is separated from the group or its mate, and before and during covey moves. Often repeated 10 or more times (70%, Edgewood notes from Calkins et al. 1999).</li><li>Audubon writes it \"ka kah ko\" or \"Chi ca go\", the second note highest <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. The BC atlas writes \"put way doo\" <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Contact calls: soft notes that keep a feeding covey together <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>. Washington Fish and Wildlife: listen for soft clucking while they feed <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Alarm: a quiet \"pit pit\" warning (60%, Okanagan naturalist in iNFOnews). The sentinel gives contact and aerial alarm calls <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Advertising call: a single loud \"cow\" from a high perch, by unpaired males early in the breeding season <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Fighting call: \"squill\", between males sorting out rank in spring <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation, top view. A strip of brush with open ground past its end. You walk along the brush from the left. The covey runs ahead of you inside the cover. When the cover runs out, the birds burst into the air and fan out over the open. Quail run rather than fly, 70 percent. Tip: be ready at the end of the cover.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">They run first, then fly</text>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"210\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<rect x=\"40\" y=\"110\" width=\"250\" height=\"60\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"165\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">strip of brush</text>\n<text x=\"345\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">open</text>\n<g><g transform=\"translate(0 0)\"><circle r=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"0\" y=\"-16\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You</text></g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"20 196;200 196;200 196\" keyTimes=\"0;.6;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n<circle r=\"6\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"><animate attributeName=\"cx\" values=\"90;270;270;340;340\" keyTimes=\"0;.55;.62;.8;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><animate attributeName=\"cy\" values=\"126;126;126;70;70\" keyTimes=\"0;.55;.62;.8;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></circle>\n<circle r=\"6\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"><animate attributeName=\"cx\" values=\"102;274;274;350;350\" keyTimes=\"0;.55;.62;.8;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><animate attributeName=\"cy\" values=\"140;140;140;100;100\" keyTimes=\"0;.55;.62;.8;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></circle>\n<circle r=\"6\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"><animate attributeName=\"cx\" values=\"114;278;278;360;360\" keyTimes=\"0;.55;.62;.8;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><animate attributeName=\"cy\" values=\"154;154;154;130;130\" keyTimes=\"0;.55;.62;.8;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></circle>\n<circle r=\"6\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"><animate attributeName=\"cx\" values=\"126;282;282;370;370\" keyTimes=\"0;.55;.62;.8;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><animate attributeName=\"cy\" values=\"134;134;134;160;160\" keyTimes=\"0;.55;.62;.8;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></circle>\n<circle r=\"6\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"><animate attributeName=\"cx\" values=\"138;286;286;380;380\" keyTimes=\"0;.55;.62;.8;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><animate attributeName=\"cy\" values=\"148;148;148;190;190\" keyTimes=\"0;.55;.62;.8;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></circle>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"256\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"279\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You walk the brush. The covey runs ahead.</text>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"5.2s\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"256\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"279\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cover runs out: they burst into the air</text></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"7.4s\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"256\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"279\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Be ready at the END of the cover (Tip)</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>A covey runs ahead inside the cover, then bursts at the end. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>First choice: run. Fly as a last resort <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Cover runs out, or you get too close: they burst <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: alarm and flight in full</summary><ul><li>\"Remain on ground and run very rapidly, flying as last resort.\" (70%, Birder's Handbook)</li><li>If startled they explode into short, fast flight; given a choice, they escape on foot <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>How close before they flush: no published number for BC birds. It depends on cover, pressure and the sentinel (Tip, <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>).</li><li>Pressured birds near trees may fly up and perch in the branches (75%, Washington Fish and Wildlife).</li><li>Hunter meaning: push them toward the end of the cover, not into a big thicket. Cover too big and they just run or stay in it (75%, Washington Fish and Wildlife).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation, top view. A covey of quail hides in a clump of brush. You walk up. The covey flushes and the birds scatter in every direction, landing alone in different patches of cover. After a while the scattered birds call and walk back together to regroup in one patch. Tip: mark where they land.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#8a9a6b\"><ellipse cx=\"200\" cy=\"150\" rx=\"46\" ry=\"30\"/><ellipse cx=\"70\" cy=\"70\" rx=\"30\" ry=\"20\"/><ellipse cx=\"330\" cy=\"70\" rx=\"34\" ry=\"22\"/><ellipse cx=\"80\" cy=\"240\" rx=\"34\" ry=\"22\"/><ellipse cx=\"320\" cy=\"236\" rx=\"30\" ry=\"20\"/></g>\n  <g><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(1.0)\"><circle r=\"9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"0\" y=\"-18\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You</text></g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"200 290;200 220;200 220\" keyTimes=\"0;.3;1\" dur=\"10s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n  <g><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.5)\"><ellipse rx=\"16\" ry=\"11\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><circle cx=\"13\" cy=\"-9\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M12 -15 Q16 -26 22 -22\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/></g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"190 144;190 144;70 66;70 66;330 64\" keyTimes=\"0;.3;.42;.72;1\" dur=\"10s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n  <g><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.5)\"><ellipse rx=\"16\" ry=\"11\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><circle cx=\"13\" cy=\"-9\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M12 -15 Q16 -26 22 -22\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/></g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"197 144;197 144;330 64;330 64;338 64\" keyTimes=\"0;.3;.42;.72;1\" dur=\"10s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n  <g><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.5)\"><ellipse rx=\"16\" ry=\"11\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><circle cx=\"13\" cy=\"-9\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M12 -15 Q16 -26 22 -22\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/></g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"204 144;204 144;80 236;80 236;346 64\" keyTimes=\"0;.3;.42;.72;1\" dur=\"10s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n  <g><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.5)\"><ellipse rx=\"16\" ry=\"11\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><circle cx=\"13\" cy=\"-9\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M12 -15 Q16 -26 22 -22\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/></g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"211 144;211 144;320 232;320 232;354 64\" keyTimes=\"0;.3;.42;.72;1\" dur=\"10s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n  <g><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.5)\"><ellipse rx=\"16\" ry=\"11\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><circle cx=\"13\" cy=\"-9\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M12 -15 Q16 -26 22 -22\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/></g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"190 154;190 154;40 150;40 150;330 74\" keyTimes=\"0;.3;.42;.72;1\" dur=\"10s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n  <g><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.5)\"><ellipse rx=\"16\" ry=\"11\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><circle cx=\"13\" cy=\"-9\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M12 -15 Q16 -26 22 -22\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/></g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"197 154;197 154;360 150;360 150;338 74\" keyTimes=\"0;.3;.42;.72;1\" dur=\"10s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n  <g><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.5)\"><ellipse rx=\"16\" ry=\"11\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><circle cx=\"13\" cy=\"-9\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M12 -15 Q16 -26 22 -22\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/></g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"204 154;204 154;150 40;150 40;346 74\" keyTimes=\"0;.3;.42;.72;1\" dur=\"10s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n  <g><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.5)\"><ellipse rx=\"16\" ry=\"11\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><circle cx=\"13\" cy=\"-9\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M12 -15 Q16 -26 22 -22\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/></g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"211 154;211 154;250 36;250 36;354 74\" keyTimes=\"0;.3;.42;.72;1\" dur=\"10s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"3s\"/><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"4.4s\"/><path d=\"M160 120 l-14 -10 M170 108 l-6 -16 M230 108 l6 -16 M240 120 l14 -10\"/></g>\n  <rect x=\"10\" y=\"10\" width=\"380\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" opacity=\".92\"/>\n  <g><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"3s\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A covey hides in the brush</text></g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"3s\"/><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"7.2s\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Flush: they scatter every way</text></g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"7.2s\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Later they call and regroup (Tip)</text></g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"9.6s\"/><rect x=\"200\" y=\"96\" width=\"190\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"295\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mark where they land</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>The covey scatters, then calls and walks back together. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>A flushed covey scatters. Singles land a few dozen yards away and sit tight <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Then they call to regroup with the assembly call <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: scatter and regroup in full</summary><ul><li>\"When they scatter, quail may fly long distances, never to be seen again (at least not that day), or they may settle to the ground only a few dozen yards away\" (75%, Washington Fish and Wildlife).</li><li>\"Those singles and doubles will sometimes hold very tight once they hit the ground\" <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>\"When a covey is scattered, birds will often emit a sort of crowing whistle to locate each other, and a chorus of such calls may erupt around dusk, as birds begin to roost for the night.\" <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></li><li>An Okanagan naturalist: about 10 minutes after a flush the covey has collected itself and is pecking again (Tip, one observer, iNFOnews).</li><li>Assembly calls also start the covey's move off the night roost in the morning (70%, Edgewood notes).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Timeline after a covey flush. 0 minutes: the birds scatter. Next: singles land a few dozen yards away, Washington Fish and Wildlife, 75 percent. Then they sit tight and are hard to see. Soon assembly calls start, chi CA go, 70 percent. At dusk a chorus of calls as they gather to roost, 75 percent. One Okanagan naturalist says a covey is back together in about 10 minutes, a Tip.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">After the flush: scatter, then regroup</text>\n<line x1=\"70\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"250\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"4\"/>\n<circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"55\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"56\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">0 min</text>\n<text x=\"88\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Flush: birds scatter</text>\n<circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"100\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"56\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">next</text>\n<text x=\"88\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Singles land a few dozen yards off (75%)</text>\n<circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"145\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"56\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">then</text>\n<text x=\"88\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">They sit tight, hard to see (75%)</text>\n<circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"190\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n<text x=\"56\" y=\"195\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">soon</text>\n<text x=\"88\" y=\"195\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Assembly calls start: &quot;chi CA go&quot; (70%)</text>\n<circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"235\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"56\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">dusk</text>\n<text x=\"88\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Calling chorus as they roost (75%)</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"262\" width=\"380\" height=\"32\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">One naturalist: back together in about 10 min (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Flush, scatter, sit tight, call, regroup (70 to 75%).</li><li>Late in the day, give them time to gather before dark (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why time matters</summary><ul><li>Singles hold tight right after the flush: your best shooting chance on singles <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>As calls start, birds move toward each other. Waiting too long means they are a covey again, and wary (Tip).</li><li>Tall Timbers' Bill Palmer (bobwhite research): \"The evidence suggests it's OK to hunt singles... They are so good at getting back together.\" (60%, bobwhite, Garden and Gun 2022)</li><li>Same source, a manners rule: stop a bit before dark and give the birds time to gather (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Diagram of rings around a hunter. The first flush is close, the second flush farther, the third farther still. Washington Fish and Wildlife says gray partridge flush farther on each approach, and pressured quail near trees may fly up and perch, 75 percent. Lesson: make the first chance count.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Pressure teaches them: each flush is farther</text>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"190\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(50 140)\"><circle r=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"0\" y=\"-16\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You</text></g>\n<path d=\"M50 84.0 A70 56.0 0 0 1 50 196.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 6\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(120 150) scale(0.6 0.6)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#8f9396\"/><path d=\"M-18 -2 L-27 -4 L-25 5 Z\" fill=\"#b5652b\"/><path d=\"M-6 4 q6 -6 12 0 q-6 4 -12 0 Z\" fill=\"#6b3a1e\"/><circle cx=\"16\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#d9822b\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-13\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M23 -12 l4 1 l-4 2 Z\" fill=\"#555\"/><path d=\"M2 12 l-2 7 M8 12 l2 7\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<text x=\"120\" y=\"182\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1st</text>\n<path d=\"M50 52 A130 88 0 0 1 50 228\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 6\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(180 130) scale(0.6 0.6)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#8f9396\"/><path d=\"M-18 -2 L-27 -4 L-25 5 Z\" fill=\"#b5652b\"/><path d=\"M-6 4 q6 -6 12 0 q-6 4 -12 0 Z\" fill=\"#6b3a1e\"/><circle cx=\"16\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#d9822b\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-13\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M23 -12 l4 1 l-4 2 Z\" fill=\"#555\"/><path d=\"M2 12 l-2 7 M8 12 l2 7\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<text x=\"180\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2nd</text>\n<path d=\"M50 52 A200 88 0 0 1 50 228\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#a33b2a\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 6\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(250 110) scale(0.6 0.6)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#8f9396\"/><path d=\"M-18 -2 L-27 -4 L-25 5 Z\" fill=\"#b5652b\"/><path d=\"M-6 4 q6 -6 12 0 q-6 4 -12 0 Z\" fill=\"#6b3a1e\"/><circle cx=\"16\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#d9822b\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-13\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M23 -12 l4 1 l-4 2 Z\" fill=\"#555\"/><path d=\"M2 12 l-2 7 M8 12 l2 7\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<text x=\"250\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3rd</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"252\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Huns: farther on the 2nd and 3rd approach (75%)</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"274\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Quail near trees may fly up and perch (75%)</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">So: make the first chance count (75%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Each flush teaches them. The second flush is farther out <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Hard hunted birds hold less and run more <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: pressure in full</summary><ul><li>Gray partridge: \"after they've been flushed once, they're likely to flush farther in front of you or your dog on the second approach, still farther out on the third.\" (75%, Washington Fish and Wildlife)</li><li>Quail that have not been hunted hard may hold in small patches of cover instead of breaking into the open <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>\"Heavy hunting pressure can change the birds' habits, even moving them off an area.\" (60%, Missouri Conservationist 1996, bobwhite)</li><li>Under raptor pressure, quail feed closer to cover and may skip the afternoon feed (70%, Edgewood notes).</li><li>Hunter meaning: rest a covey. Hunt it once, then leave it a week (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bar chart of covey size. BC usual: under 30 birds, BC Breeding Bird Atlas, 85 percent. California average: 20 to 25, 70 percent. Washington: a dozen to several dozen, 75 percent. BC big coveys: 100 or more at times, 85 percent. Tip: coveys merge in hard winters.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">How many birds in a covey?</text>\n<text x=\"122\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">BC, usual</text>\n<rect x=\"132.3\" y=\"50\" width=\"66.69999999999999\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"207.0\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">under 30 (85%)</text>\n<text x=\"122\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">California avg</text>\n<rect x=\"176.0\" y=\"96\" width=\"11.5\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"195.5\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">20 to 25 (70%)</text>\n<text x=\"122\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Washington</text>\n<rect x=\"157.6\" y=\"142\" width=\"82.79999999999998\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"248.39999999999998\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">a dozen to several dozen (75%)</text>\n<text x=\"122\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">BC, big ones</text>\n<rect x=\"360.0\" y=\"188\" width=\"8\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#a33b2a\"/>\n<text x=\"354.0\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">100 or more (85%)</text>\n<line x1=\"130\" y1=\"236\" x2=\"384\" y2=\"236\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<line x1=\"130.0\" y1=\"236\" x2=\"130.0\" y2=\"242\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"130.0\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0</text>\n<line x1=\"187.5\" y1=\"236\" x2=\"187.5\" y2=\"242\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"187.5\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25</text>\n<line x1=\"245.0\" y1=\"236\" x2=\"245.0\" y2=\"242\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"245.0\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50</text>\n<line x1=\"302.5\" y1=\"236\" x2=\"302.5\" y2=\"242\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"302.5\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75</text>\n<line x1=\"360.0\" y1=\"236\" x2=\"360.0\" y2=\"242\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"360.0\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100</text>\n<text x=\"256\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">birds per covey</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"296\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Coveys merge in hard winters (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Fall coveys: often under 30, sometimes 100 or more in BC <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Males hold a rank order. Only ranked males get mates <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: social life in full</summary><ul><li>BC: coveys \"occasionally include 100 or more birds, but more frequently less than 30\" (85%, BC Breeding Bird Atlas).</li><li>California: coveys average 20 to 25 (70%, Edgewood notes); up to 200, rarely over 300, in fall and winter (70%, Birder's Handbook).</li><li>Washington: a dozen to several dozen birds <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. Over 1,000 birds together has been reported in BC in fall and winter (Tip, search preview of Sierra Club BC, <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>).</li><li>Families merge: broods join into \"communal broods\" with several adults (60%, Wikipedia summary).</li><li>Males have dominance hierarchies that shape mate choice, relations between coveys and brood moves. Only birds in the hierarchy get mates. Dominant birds call more (70%, Edgewood notes).</li><li>Pairs form from birds of the same covey. If both survive, they tend to pair again the next year <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>In good years a female may lay a second clutch, leaving the first brood with a male <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bar chart from an early California banding study, 60 percent, search preview. Of 101 quail banded, 52 were known alive at 6 months, 15 at 1 year, 4 at 2 years and 1 at 3 years. Lesson: most quail in a fall covey are young of the year.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Few quail live long (early banding study)</text>\n<line x1=\"60\" y1=\"240\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<line x1=\"60\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"60\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<rect x=\"80\" y=\"68.30000000000001\" width=\"44\" height=\"171.7\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"102\" y=\"62.30000000000001\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">101</text>\n<text x=\"102\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">start</text>\n<rect x=\"142\" y=\"151.60000000000002\" width=\"44\" height=\"88.39999999999999\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"164\" y=\"145.60000000000002\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">52</text>\n<text x=\"164\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">6 mo</text>\n<rect x=\"204\" y=\"214.5\" width=\"44\" height=\"25.5\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"226\" y=\"208.5\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">15</text>\n<text x=\"226\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1 yr</text>\n<rect x=\"266\" y=\"233.2\" width=\"44\" height=\"6.8\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"288\" y=\"227.2\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4</text>\n<text x=\"288\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2 yr</text>\n<rect x=\"328\" y=\"238.3\" width=\"44\" height=\"1.7\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"350\" y=\"232.3\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1</text>\n<text x=\"350\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3 yr</text>\n<text x=\"220\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">101 birds banded: how many were still seen (60%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Older birds pair earlier. Adult hens pick adult cocks <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Most fall birds are young: they have never seen a hunter (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: old and young in full</summary><ul><li>\"Older birds generally mate earlier than younger birds, and adult females generally mate with adult males rather than yearling males.\" (70%, Edgewood notes)</li><li>Few quail live past one year <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>. An old bird in your bag is uncommon (Tip).</li><li>Tip: early October coveys full of young often hold better than the same coveys in late November after a few flushes.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>They always...</th><th>So you... (Tip)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Call at dawn and dusk</td><td>Listen first, hunt next morning</td></tr><tr><td>Run to the end of cover</td><td>Be ready where it ends</td></tr><tr><td>Hold tight as singles</td><td>Hunt singles right after the flush</td></tr><tr><td>Dust and pick grit on lanes</td><td>Check lane edges midday and early</td></tr><tr><td>Come back to the same cover</td><td>Mark it in the Journal and on the map</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Habits are strong; the covey is predictable (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: where the table comes from</summary><ul><li>Dawn and dusk calling: Edgewood notes and Washington Fish and Wildlife (70 to 75%).</li><li>Running ahead in cover: Birder's Handbook <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Singles hold tight: Washington Fish and Wildlife <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Grit and dusting on road edges: Washington Fish and Wildlife <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Same small range: California winter home range of four coveys averaged 10.5 ha, from 6.9 to 18 ha (80%, California wildlife habitat records).</li><li>\"Quail often return to the same areas\" (Tip, hunting articles).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Timeline after a covey flush. 0 minutes: the birds scatter. Next: singles land a few dozen yards away, Washington Fish and Wildlife, 75 percent. Then they sit tight and are hard to see. Soon assembly calls start, chi CA go, 70 percent. At dusk a chorus of calls as they gather to roost, 75 percent. One Okanagan naturalist says a covey is back together in about 10 minutes, a Tip.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">After the flush: scatter, then regroup</text>\n<line x1=\"70\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"250\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"4\"/>\n<circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"55\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"56\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">0 min</text>\n<text x=\"88\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Flush: birds scatter</text>\n<circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"100\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"56\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">next</text>\n<text x=\"88\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Singles land a few dozen yards off (75%)</text>\n<circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"145\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"56\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">then</text>\n<text x=\"88\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">They sit tight, hard to see (75%)</text>\n<circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"190\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n<text x=\"56\" y=\"195\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">soon</text>\n<text x=\"88\" y=\"195\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Assembly calls start: &quot;chi CA go&quot; (70%)</text>\n<circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"235\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"56\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">dusk</text>\n<text x=\"88\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Calling chorus as they roost (75%)</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"262\" width=\"380\" height=\"32\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">One naturalist: back together in about 10 min (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Flush and scatter, sit and wait; then chi CA go calls up the mate.\" (Tip)</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> \"10, 30, 10\": regroup in about 10 min (Tip), coveys under 30 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>, winter range about 10 ha <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li><strong>Script:</strong> watch, call, run, burst, scatter, regroup. Six words, the whole mind <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule (opinion):</strong> \"Three birds from a covey, then let it go.\" A traditional manners rule quoted by Tall Timbers' Bill Palmer (Tip, 60%).</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule (opinion):</strong> \"Listen at dusk, hunt at dawn.\" Widely repeated in quail hunting guides (Tip, Washington Fish and Wildlife describes the dusk chorus, 75%).</li></ul></details>","<ul><li>Edgewood notes (from Calkins et al. 1999), Washington Fish and Wildlife, BC Breeding Bird Atlas, Birder's Handbook, Garden and Gun with Tall Timbers. Checked 2026-10-11.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every source and date checked</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://friendsofedgewood.org/?p=5231\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Friends of Edgewood: California quail (Franks 2002, summarizing Calkins, Hagelin and Lott 1999, The Birds of North America 473)</a>, read directly 2026-10-11: calls, sentinel, hierarchy, pairing, feeding <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://wdfw.wa.gov/node/68963\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Washington Fish and Wildlife: quail hunting</a> and <a href=\"https://wdfw.wa.gov/node/68921\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">gray partridge hunting</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.birdatlas.bc.ca/accounts/speciesaccount.jsp?sp=CAQU&amp;lang=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC Breeding Bird Atlas, California quail</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.audubon.org/field-guide/bird/california-quail\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Audubon field guide: California quail</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://web.stanford.edu/group/stanfordbirds/text/species/California_Quail.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Stanford Birds (Birder's Handbook)</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://ncrcd.specialdistrict.org/files/b900df31f/California-Quail-info.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">California Wildlife Habitat Relationships: California quail</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://gardenandgun.com/southern-conundrum-is-it-okay-to-hunt-singles-after-you-flush-a-covey-of-quail\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Garden and Gun: hunting singles after a covey flush (Nickens 2022, quoting Bill Palmer of Tall Timbers)</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 (60%, bobwhite).</li><li><a href=\"https://infonews.ca/?p=13774\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">iNFOnews 2018</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>. <a href=\"https://mdc.mo.gov/node/245855\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Missouri Conservationist 1996</a>, read directly <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California_quail\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikipedia: California quail</a>, read directly 2026-10-11, used only for communal broods <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>. Sierra Club BC page: search preview only (<span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>).</li></ul></details>"]